   $q$How is the fable organized?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tull tells the story of his dam to three animals after it is finished.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"Tull asks three animals the same question, and the third answer differs.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Three young beavers each build a dam in a different way at once.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The old beaver describes the three dams she built when she was young.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tull asks three animals the same question, and the third answer differs.$q$, $q$Tull visits the heron, the otter and the old beaver in turn, asking each the same question, and only the third does not offer a shortcut. Tull is the one asking, not telling a finished story.$q$, 'draft', '2366d6b8-56e8-5831-85db-6109c8562e2c')
