-- Passage rg8-literary-structure-pov-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('c25ef29e-8373-54c9-891b-bb2e40e7550d', 'rg8-literary-structure-pov-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Final Run$q$, $q$A middle school gym during a robotics competition. Three teammates, DEV, MARISOL and AUGUST, stand behind a taped square. Their robot, a boxy machine nicknamed Pickle, waits on the starting line. Unseen by the team, a small battery clip on Pickle's back hangs loose.

ANNOUNCER: Team Fourteen, you have ninety seconds. Begin when ready.

DEV: (whispering) This is it. If Pickle stacks all six blocks, we go to regionals.

MARISOL: (holding the controller) Relax. We tested it twenty times this morning. Nothing can go wrong.

(AUGUST leans close to Pickle and frowns, but a judge waves him back behind the tape.)

AUGUST: Wait, I think something is...

ANNOUNCER: Three, two, one, go!

(Pickle rolls forward and grabs the first block. The battery clip wiggles with each bump.)

DEV: One! Two! It's perfect!

(Pickle lifts the third block. Its lights flicker for half a second.)

MARISOL: Did anyone else see that?

DEV: See what? Keep going!

(The fourth and fifth blocks land on the stack. The clip slides farther out.)

AUGUST: (quietly) Marisol, drive slower. Trust me.

(MARISOL eases off the controller. Pickle creeps toward the last block, places it gently, and stops. A second later, the clip drops to the floor with a small click, and every light on Pickle goes dark.)

ANNOUNCER: Six blocks! Time!

(The team stares at the dark robot, then at the clip on the floor, then at each other.)

DEV: Okay. Nobody tell Pickle how close that was.$q$, 'draft')
