   $q$Which statement best compares how the two structures affect the reader?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Part One focuses on Amir's feelings about the patch, while Part Two focuses only on the clock times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Both parts build the same suspense, because each one follows the events in the exact same order.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-structural-difference"},{"text":"Part One reveals the happy ending first, while Part Two keeps the reader guessing until the final line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"Part One builds suspense about the kite, while Part Two removes it early and focuses on why the day mattered.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Part One builds suspense about the kite, while Part Two removes it early and focuses on why the day mattered.$q$, $q$In Part One the reader wonders if the kite is "gone forever" until noon, but Part Two tells Leila at once that the kite is safe and patched, shifting attention to its meaning. Part One never mentions the patch, so it does not reveal the ending first.$q$, 'draft', '5154a87c-f315-53d4-9481-7d758b9e0a2a')
